Bullywugcroak is the croaking, bubbling language of bullywugs and frogfolk.
It consists of deep-throated croaks, clicks, and watery burbles that carry
well across swamps and marshlands where these amphibious creatures dwell.

Much of the language involves rhythm and timing, with meaning conveyed through
the pattern of croaks as much as their sound. Speakers often puff their
throat pouches to add emphasis or indicate emotional state.

Understanding Bullywugcroak is essential when venturing into swamplands
controlled by bullywug tribes. These creatures are territorial and often
hostile, but those who speak their tongue may find opportunities for trade
or safe passage.

